  finish with args {'message': 'Successfully generated test case for CVE-2023-0358 (heap-use-after-free in gf_odf_vvc_cfg_read_bs).\n\n**Test Case Location**: /home/ubuntu/PoV/DrillAgent/workspace-sonnet/gpac.cve-2023-0358/round2/testcase-round2.mp4\n\n**Vulnerability Summary**:\nThe vulnerability is a heap-use-after-free in `gf_odf_vvc_cfg_read_bs()` at line 1403. When parsing a VVC configuration box with an invalid NALU array type, the code frees the `ar` pointer in the `default:` case but then immediately dereferences it to check `ar->type`.\n\n**Key Improvements from Round 1**:\n1. **Fixed PTL parsing**: Round 1 failed because the vvcC box ran out of bytes before reaching the NALU array loop. The parser read PTL data (ptl_present was 1) but insufficient data was provided.\n2. **Proper PTL data**: This test case provides complete PTL (Profile, Tier, Level) data including all required fields (ols_idx, numTemporalLayers, profile_idc, level_idc, etc.) to satisfy the parser and reach line 1370 where `count` is read.\n3. **Invalid NALU type**: Set NALU array type to 0 (not in valid switch cases: DEC_PARAM, OPI, VID_PARAM, SEQ_PARAM, PIC_PARAM, SEI_PREFIX, SEI_SUFFIX), triggering the `default:` case that frees `ar` at line 1399.\n4. **UAF trigger**: After freeing `ar`, the code at line 1403 dereferences `ar->type`, causing the heap-use-after-free crash.\n\n**Test Case Structure**:\n- Valid MP4 file with ftyp, moov, trak, mdia, minf, stbl boxes\n- VVC video sample entry (vvc1) in stsd box\n- vvcC configuration box with:\n  - ptl_present = 1 with complete PTL data\n  - count = 1 (one NALU array)\n  - NALU array type = 0 (invalid, triggers UAF)\n  - Dummy NALU data to avoid early termination\n\nThe test case should successfully reach `gf_odf_vvc_cfg_read_bs()` and trigger the use-after-free vulnerability.', 'task_completed': 'true'}


